# Per-image Trivy override file for spectre-playwright.
# See tools/trivy/README.md for usage criteria.
#
# Format: one CVE ID per line, '#'-prefixed comments allowed.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Microsoft Playwright runtime base image findings (W1.3, 2026-05-07)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The five CVEs below live in Microsoft's `mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:
# v1.59.1-noble` base image's own node_modules tree (Playwright CLI tooling
# bundled with the image), not in our pnpm-managed dependencies. Verified
# locally: adding pnpm.overrides for minimatch / picomatch / tar in
# adapters/playwright/package.json has no effect on Trivy's findings —
# Trivy's `(package.json)` annotation points at Microsoft's bundled
# package.json, not ours.
#
# Outside our control until Microsoft publishes a newer Playwright base
# image that picks up the upstream npm fixes. Tracking via:
# - https://hub.docker.com/_/microsoft-playwright (image version watch)
# - bumping `PLAYWRIGHT_VERSION` in build/docker/versions.env when a base
#   image with the fixes lands
#
# All five are DoS-class (denial-of-service via crafted regex / glob /
# archive paths). The Playwright adapter does not parse user-supplied
# regex / glob / tar input from external sources — these CVEs surface in
# Playwright's CLI tooling (test runner, browser-installer scripts) that
# do not run in the production adapter container at runtime. Risk of
# real-world exploitation in our deployment shape: low.
#
# Reviewed: 2026-05-07 by maintainer (W1.3 PR #101).

# minimatch: Denial of Service due to unbounded recursive backtracking.
# Fix available in upstream minimatch >= 10.2.3.
CVE-2026-27903

# minimatch: Denial of Service via catastrophic backtracking in glob
# expressions. Fix available in upstream minimatch >= 10.2.3.
CVE-2026-27904

# picomatch: Regular Expression Denial of Service via crafted extglob
# patterns. Fix available in upstream picomatch >= 4.0.4.
CVE-2026-33671

# node-tar: hardlink path traversal via drive-relative linkpath. Fix
# available in upstream tar >= 7.5.10.
CVE-2026-29786

# tar: File overwrite via drive-relative symlink traversal. Fix
# available in upstream tar >= 7.5.11.
CVE-2026-31802
